-// helium-fork: the one owner of the Arc card's outline.
-//
-// The card -- the address bar band and the page below it -- is a rounded
-// rectangle floating 3pt inside the window, and unlike the classic layout it
-// has nothing that clips it: there the rounded shape *is* the window, and the
-// window clips everything, so the band, the page and the frame cannot disagree
-// about it. Here every part painted its own arc of the corner and they agreed
-// only as long as the arithmetic happened to line up. It did not line up during
-// the zen reveal: the band's corner radius is applied to the band's own rect,
-// and Skia scales a radius down to fit a short rect (SkRRect::setRectRadii), so
-// while the band grows 0 -> 34pt its corners are drawn at roughly its own
-// height. For the first frames of every reveal the card had square corners
-// ("在呼出地址栏的第一帧…ui会先变成直角，然后再完成动画").
-//
-// This view is laid out to exactly the card and paints the surrounding plane
-// back over everything outside the card's rounded rect. That is subtractive:
-// it can only remove what a part painted beyond the outline, never add. So the
-// card's silhouette is *by construction* the one rounded rect that
-// helium::ComputeArcCardLayout() describes -- at any band height, in any
-// address bar mode, with or without an infobar or a split view -- instead of
-// being the coincidence of several parts agreeing.
-//
-// The other half of the contract lives elsewhere and is worth stating here:
-// this view cannot fill a *gap* (a part painting less than the outline). That
-// is what the single attachment predicate, ArcCardLayout::band_occupies_card_
-// top(), is for -- the page drops its top inset and its top corners exactly
-// when the band takes over the card's top edge.
-//
-// Ordering in BrowserView's children is load-bearing; see the AddChildView call
-// in browser_view.cc.
-class ArcCardOutlineView : public views::View {
-  METADATA_HEADER(ArcCardOutlineView, views::View)
-
- public:
-  explicit ArcCardOutlineView(BrowserView* browser_view);
-  ArcCardOutlineView(const ArcCardOutlineView&) = delete;
-  ArcCardOutlineView& operator=(const ArcCardOutlineView&) = delete;
-  ~ArcCardOutlineView() override;
-
-  // The card's corner radius. Must come from ArcCardLayout::corner_radius so
-  // the outline and the geometry cannot drift apart; zero disables painting.
-  void SetCornerRadius(int corner_radius);
-  int corner_radius() const { return corner_radius_; }
-
-  // views::View:
-  void OnPaint(gfx::Canvas* canvas) override;
-  // The wedges are the window's plane color; this view owns a layer, so the
-  // theme change has to invalidate it explicitly or the corners keep the old
-  // color (see the .cc).
-  void OnThemeChanged() override;
-
- private:
-  const raw_ptr<BrowserView> browser_view_;
-  int corner_radius_ = 0;
-};
-
-#endif  // CHROME_BROWSER_UI_VIEWS_FRAME_ARC_CARD_OUTLINE_VIEW_H_
